Product Track
--------------
Program that track prices on websites, using a headless browser. To automate the program, it can be installed as a daemon service in Linux enviroments.

Requirements
-------------
 - Golang 1.25.6
 - Postgresql Database
 - Golang package go-rod/rod 0.116.2
 - Browser (Chrome, Edge, Opera, FireFox)

How to use it
--------------
1. Compile the source code to obtain a single standalone executable binary.
```bash
go build .
```

2. Run the executable binary
```bash
go run product-tracking
```

How to install as a daemon service
------------------------------------
1. Move the .env file and the binary generated on the previous statement to a dedicated path.
```bash
mkdir /ptrack
mv product-tracking /ptrack/
mv .env /ptrack/
```

2. Create a file in the path "/etc/systemd/system/" with the following content.

```bash
# file name product-track.service
[Unit]
Description=track online product prices
After=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=simple
User={os_user}
WorkingDirectory=/ptrack/
ExecStart=/ptrack/product-tracking
Restart=on-failure
RestartSec=60
StandardOutput=append:/ptrack/ptrack.log
StandardError=append:/ptrack/ptrack.log

#Grant permission to low ports withput root user
CapabilityBoundingSet=CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE CAP_DAC_OVERRIDE
AmbientCapabilities=CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE CAP_DAC_OVERRIDE CAP_DAC_READ_SEARCH CAP_CHOWN CAP_FOWNER CAP_SYS_CHROOT CAP_SYS_PTRACE CAP_SYS_ADMIN

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
```

3. Create and run the new daemon service
```bash
sudo systemctl enable product-track.service
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl start product-track.service
```

4. Verify the status of the new service
```bash
sudo systemctl status product-track.service
```

Things to consider
-------------------
On most Linux distros, apt install chromium installs a snap wrapper, not a real browser. Install Google Chrome directly from its binaries.
```bash
wget https://dl.google.com/linux/direct/google-chrome-stable_current_amd64.deb
sudo dpkg -i google-chrome-stable_current_amd64.deb
sudo apt --fix-broken install -y
```
Or
``` bash
sudo apt install ./google-chrome-stable_current_amd64.deb
```